    "turn_text": "Talk about that a little bit. I was mostly interested in sports. I played baseball. As a little boy and then I played basketball once I realized I'm gonna be taller than most kids by the time I was in middle school and high school as well. We did have a very good junior RTC program by two good men, veterans themselves, Lieutenant Colonel. And why did you join me? It was very common, very popular program. So it was probably the single biggest extracurricular activity we had in the school. But no sense at that point that you wanted to join the Army somebody? No, I thought about it at different times. But it was just, like I said, it was very common, boy and girl alike. Most athletes did it. Frankly, it was a recruiting tool for some athletes, because you could come from the smaller, less competitive high schools across the county if there was a program that a public school had that your school lacked. And we had more of the RGC program in the county. So we",
